            <ArticleTitle>[Coxalgia in adolescents: apropos of three different cases: chondrolysis, transient osteoporosis and epiphyseolysis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>182-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report 3 adolescents presenting with hip pain. Idiopathic chondrolysis, transient osteoporosis and slipped epiphisis were the final diagnosis. Initial diagnosis may be difficult despite adequate investigation. In such cases long-term follow-up is essential. This paper includes a differential diagnosis of hip problems in childhood.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
